." $NetBSD$
.Dd February 13, 2026
.Dt CELLMGR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cellmgr
.Nd provision and manage multiple cellctl cells from one configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a shell-script helper around
.Xr cellctl 8
for provisioning and operating multiple cells.
It is designed for setups that use:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
a shared, read-only base filesystem extracted from
.Pa base.tar.xz ,
.It
a per-cell writable
.Pa /.data
mount for mutable state (with base-layer symlinks from
.Pa /etc ,
.Pa /var ,
.Pa /tmp ,
.Pa /home ,
.Pa /root ,
and
.Pa /usr/pkg
into
.Pa /.data ) ,
a cell-local
.Pa /dev ,
and
.It
cell naming and lifecycle management via
.Xr cellctl 8 .
.El
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
reads configuration from
.Pa /etc/cellmgr.conf .
A different configuration file can be selected with the
.Ev CELLMGR_CONF
environment variable.
.Pp
Most commands require superuser privileges.
.Sh COMMANDS
The following commands are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "restart --all"
.It Cm bootstrap
Download
.Pa base.tar.xz
and
.Pa etc.tar.xz
from
.Ev NETBSD_MIRROR
after ensuring the
.Li secmodel_cell
kernel module is loaded,
and persist
.Li secmodel_cell
in
.Pa /etc/modules.conf
for future boots.
Also ensure
.Li cellmgr=
exists in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
and initialize it to
.Dq NO
if absent.
If
.Pa /etc/cellmgr.conf
does not exist, create it using the running system release normalized to
.Dq major.minor
.Pq e.g. Dq 10.1
so mirror URLs do not include suffixes like
.Dq _STABLE
or
.Dq _RC1 .
Then
extract
.Pa base.tar.xz
into the configured shared base layer directory.
.It Cm create Op Fl a Op Fl x Ar cmd Op Fl l Ar profile Op Fl r Ar port[,port...] Op Fl f Ar facility Op Fl o Ar stdout-level Op Fl e Ar stderr-level Op Fl t Ar tag Ar name
Create directories and metadata for one cell:
.Pa root ,
.Pa data ,
and
.Pa dev .
If necessary,
.Pa etc.tar.xz
is extracted for that cell, but only the
.Pa ./etc ,
.Pa ./root ,
.Pa ./var
entries are unpacked into
.Pa data/ .
For local cell
.Pa /dev
setup,
.Pa ./dev/MAKEDEV
and optional
.Pa ./dev/MAKEDEV.local
are extracted directly from
.Pa etc.tar.xz
into the cell's mounted
.Pa /dev
tmpfs.
If host
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf
exists,
it is copied to
.Pa data/etc/resolv.conf
at create time.
A cell-local shell configuration file is written to
.Pa ${CELL_DATA_DIR}/name/cell.conf .
When
.Fl a
is provided,
.Ev CELL_AUTOSTART
is initialized to
.Dq YES
in that generated
.Pa cell.conf .
When
.Fl x
is provided,
.Ev CELL_SUPERVISE_CMD
is initialized to the specified command string in the generated
.Pa cell.conf .
When
.Fl l
is provided,
the generated
.Pa cell.conf
stores the corresponding
.Xr cellctl 8
create profile
.Pq Dq low ,
.Dq medium ,
or
.Dq high .
When
.Fl r
is provided,
the generated
.Pa cell.conf
stores the corresponding
.Xr cellctl 8
create-time reserved listening ports
.Pq comma-separated list forwarded to Cm create Fl r .
When
.Fl f ,
.Fl o ,
.Fl e ,
or
.Fl t
is provided,
the generated
.Pa cell.conf
stores the corresponding
.Xr cellctl 8
supervisor logging settings.
.It Cm start Ar name
Mount the composed cell root and start the cell with
.Xr cellctl 8 , using required per-cell settings from
.Pa cell.conf .
.It Cm start Cm --all
Start all cells found under
.Ev CELL_DATA_DIR
with a
.Pa cell.conf
and
.Ev CELL_AUTOSTART=YES .
If one cell fails to start, processing continues with the next cell.
.It Cm stop Ar name
Terminate the corresponding
.Xr cellctl 8
supervise process for the cell named
.Ar name ,
then destroy the cell by name through
.Xr cellctl 8
and unmount its root composition.
.It Cm stop Cm --all
Stop and unmount all cells found under
.Ev CELL_DATA_DIR
with a
.Pa cell.conf
and
.Ev CELL_AUTOSTART=YES .
.It Cm restart Ar name
Run
.Cm stop
for cell
.Ar name
and then
.Cm start
for the same cell, using the optional settings from
.Pa cell.conf .
.It Cm restart Cm --all
Run
.Cm stop Cm --all
followed by
.Cm start Cm --all .
.It Cm apply Op Cm --ephemeral Ar name Op Ar script | Cm - Op Cm -- Ar arg ...
Execute a shell script inside cell
.Ar name
using
.Xr jexec 8
and
.Pa /bin/sh .
If the cell is not running, it is started first.
When started by
.Cm apply ,
only the cell runtime is created;
the configured
.Cm cellctl supervise
process is not launched.
The script can be provided as a filesystem path, as
.Cm -
to read from standard input, or omitted when standard input is not a terminal
.Pq for heredoc use .
The script is copied into cell
.Pa /tmp
with a unique temporary filename before execution and removed afterwards.
Arguments after
.Cm --
are passed through to the script.
By default, a cell started for
.Cm apply
remains running.
When
.Cm --ephemeral
is specified, a cell that was started by
.Cm apply
is stopped again after script execution.
.It Cm config Ar name
Open
.Pa ${CELL_DATA_DIR}/name/cell.conf
for editing in the standard editor for the current environment.
.Nm
uses
.Ev VISUAL
when set,
otherwise
.Ev EDITOR ,
and falls back to
.Cm vi .
.It Cm list
List all configured cells as a table with columns
.Li NAME ,
.Li ROOT ,
.Li SUPERVISE_CMD ,
and
.Li AUTOSTART .
.It Cm status
Show
.Xr cellctl 8
status and mount status for all configured cells.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
accepts shell-style variable assignments in
.Pa /etc/cellmgr.conf
(or the file referenced by
.Ev CELLMGR_CONF ) .
.Pp
Important variables:
.Bl -tag -width "CELL_RELEASE_DIR"
.It Ev RELEASE
NetBSD release used for set download paths, in
.Dq NetBSD release directory
form
.Pq e.g. Dq 11.0 or Dq 11.0_RC1 ; avoid branch suffixes like Dq _STABLE .
If unset or empty,
.Nm
auto-detects it from
.Xr uname 1 .
.It Ev MACHINE_ARCH
Machine architecture used for set download paths.
If unset or empty,
.Nm
auto-detects it from
.Xr uname 1 .
.It Ev NETBSD_MIRROR
Base URL for set downloads.
.It Ev CELL_BASE_DIR
Directory containing extracted shared base layers.
.It Ev CELL_DATA_DIR
Directory containing per-cell writable state.
.It Ev CELL_RELEASE_DIR
Directory containing downloaded set archives.
.It Ev CELL_LOCAL_DEV
When set to
.Dq YES
(default), mount a cell-local tmpfs on
.Pa /dev
and populate a minimal device set with
.Xr MAKEDEV 8 .
.It Ev CELL_DEV_SIZE
Size argument used for the tmpfs mounted at cell-local
.Pa /dev
(default
.Dq 8m ) .
.It Ev CELL_DEVICES
Whitespace-separated list of
.Xr MAKEDEV 8
targets used to populate cell-local
.Pa /dev .
.It Ev CELL_PTYFS
When set to
.Dq YES
(default), mount
.Xr ptyfs 5
at
.Pa /dev/pts
inside each cell-local
.Pa /dev
to support pseudo terminals.
.El
.Pp
Each cell also has a cell-local configuration file at
.Pa ${CELL_DATA_DIR}/name/cell.conf
that provides:
.Bl -tag -width "CELL_CREATE_RESERVED_PORTS"
.It Ev CELL_NAME
Cell name recorded by
.Nm
at create time.
This must match the directory name used by
.Nm
.Pq Pa ${CELL_DATA_DIR}/name/ .
.It Ev CELL_RELEASE
Release value recorded by
.Nm
at create time.
This is informational and tracks the host-side base-layer release used when
the cell was created.
.It Ev CELL_ARCH
Architecture value recorded by
.Nm
at create time.
This is informational and tracks the host-side base-layer architecture used
when the cell was created.
.It Ev CELL_AUTOSTART
When set to
.Dq YES ,
include that cell in
.Cm start --all ,
.Cm stop --all ,
and
.Cm restart --all .
.It Ev CELL_SUPERVISE_CMD
Required command (with optional arguments) passed to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm supervise
after cell creation.
Only the supervised command's stdout/stderr are forwarded to host syslog.
Programs that default to internal syslog logging (for example
.Xr bozohttpd 8
without
.Fl s )
must be configured to emit to stderr if those logs should be captured by
.Nm .
.It Ev CELL_CREATE_PROFILE
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm create Fl l
.Pq one of
.Dq low ,
.Dq medium ,
or
.Dq high .
.It Ev CELL_CREATE_RESERVED_PORTS
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm create Fl r
.Pq comma-separated TCP/UDP port list .
.It Ev CELL_SUPERVISE_FACILITY
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl f .
.It Ev CELL_SUPERVISE_STDOUT_LEVEL
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl o .
.It Ev CELL_SUPERVISE_STDERR_LEVEL
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl e .
.It Ev CELL_SUPERVISE_TAG
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr cellctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl t .
.El
.Sh POLICY AND METRICS
.Nm
persists create-time isolation policy values
.Pq profile and optional reserved-port list
in each cell's
.Pa cell.conf
and forwards them unchanged to
.Xr cellctl 8
on start.
.Pp
Runtime resource visibility is intentionally observation-only:
use
.Cm cellctl stats
to read kernel snapshot metrics per cell.
No per-cell resource admission limits are configured by
.Nm .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/share/examples/cellmgr/cellmgr.conf.sample"
.It Pa /etc/cellmgr.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/cellmgr
Service script for boot-time start/stop of autostart-enabled cells.
.It Pa /usr/share/examples/cellmgr/cellmgr.conf.sample
Sample configuration file.
.It Pa /usr/share/examples/cellmgr/README
Operational notes and quick-start guidance.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Bring a host to operational readiness and deploy one web cell:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# cellmgr bootstrap
# cellmgr create -a -x '/usr/libexec/httpd -I 8080 -X -f -s /var/www/mysite' -l medium -r 8080 -f local3 -o info -e err -t cell-web web
# cellmgr apply --ephemeral web <<'APPLY'
mkdir -p /var/www/mysite
echo "<html>Hello NetBSD!</html>" > /var/www/mysite/index.html
APPLY
# cellmgr config web
# cellmgr start --all
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
Cell isolation policy is enforced in
.Xr secmodel_cell 9
through
.Xr kauth 9
listeners.
Resource data exposed by
.Cm cellctl stats
is snapshot telemetry and does not configure admission limits.

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cellctl 8 ,
.Xr mount_null 8 ,
.Xr secmodel_cell 9 ,
